# Scan-gate pattern files. ci/scanner.sh falls back to .ci/patterns when no
# install config is present, so this directory is where a local pattern set
# lands. Those files ARE the personal-data wordlist the gate exists to protect,
# and the gate cannot reliably detect them in itself: a pattern written \bName\b
# is preceded by the alnum 'b' of its own \b, so the word-boundary form cannot
# match itself. Never commit them.
.ci/patterns/
